{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-adventure/223954-checking-to-see-if-i-bit-off-more-than-i-could-chew-with-adventure","id":223954,"title":"checking to see if I bit off more than I could chew with Adventure!","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum","Trinity Continuum: Adventure!"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-08-10T01:31:03-07:00","id":223954,"title":"checking to see if I bit off more than I could chew with Adventure!","content":"So my group wanted me to run another adventure campaign, cause we hadnt done one since mine finished about 08. I decided that I would make an epic saga. I ran 32-34 sessions of adventure in the normal timeline, then fast forwarded to the characters grandchildren playing in the mid 80's as novas, that lasted almost 30 games, and ked into the normal timeline k f the nova age-2008 to 2012ish. Then I let the players play those nova's kids from freshman year in 2025-2029 and ended with them having to stop their parents from starting the aberrant war...well...delaying it. The characters mentor was a nova who was their age when their parents were becoming the big fish. During their game, a players old nova created technology that allowed for interstelar travel to become almost mainstream...using warp, super science, mega intelligence 6 and owning the worlds largest tech company. Their mentor was lost when the ship was accidentally launched across the galaxy (he wasnt smart enough to get it back home) so...fast forward 500 years later to 2550. Ive used Adventure! Rules, along with some old nova tech, and converted a bunch of Trinity stuff to fit and made up 8 alien races to go along with humans to interact with in a Mass Effect/Firefly setting where the characters are the very distant progeny of those novas...hence they are inspired. They found an ancient derilict vessel on a backwater world after being captured by slavers and tossed through a wormhole, and ppl icked up a human passenger while they were at it...an old man who knows way too much and seems to be able to do anything (the old characters mentor was a mega stam+adaptibility whore...so long life because plot.) My grand plan is to have the characters save the galaxy from total annihilation after getting into a interstellar war and some other stuff...and to travel back in time and give a random trinket that will be &quot;magic&quot; to a person...who will turn out to be the first ever nova thay lives in an old temple like thingy that the characters originally dealt with in the old Adventure game. So...each species has a &quot;racial ability&quot; that allows them access to a knack or two without inspiration because only humans can be actually inspired, their own culture, language, means of FTL travel, territory in the known galaxy, and story hook as to why the characters want to interact with any of them. Anyone think I went too far this time? If you have any auestikns going more I to detail on stuff in this universe, ill be happy to answer any questions. Ahh, and they kept the ship because on a exceptional navigation check, they can cover over 500 light years in about .24 seconds while the rest of the galaxy has topped out at 50 per week.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=392\" data-tempid=\"temp_392_1519878565794_106\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3676-manbearpig","name":"ManBearPig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3676_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"148"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-10T01:32:25-07:00","id":223960,"title":"","content":"Im very sorry...I typed that in my phone, an